oogle Scholar ] Pagel PS, Hudetz JA. Recent trends in publication of basic science and clinical research by United States investigators in anesthesia journals. BMC Anesthesiol. 2012;12:5. doi: 10.1186/1471-2253-12-5. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Not-so-deep impact. Nature. 2005;435:1003–1004. doi: 10.1038/4351003b. doi:10.1038/4351003b. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Dissecting our impact factor. Nat Mater. 2011;10:645. doi: 10.1038/nmat3114. doi:10.1038/nmat3114. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Saha S, Saint S, Christakis DA. Impact factor: a valid measure of journal quality? J Med Libr Assoc. 2003;91:42–46. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Rezaei-Ghaleh N, Azizi F. The impact factor-based quality assessment of biomedical research institutes in Iran: effect of impact factor normalization by subject. Arch Iran Med. 2007;10:182–189. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Mimouni D, Pavlovsky L, Akerman L, David M, Mimouni FB. Trends in dermatology publications over the past 15 years. Am J Clin Dermatol. 2010;11:55–58. doi: 10.2165/11530190-000000000-00000. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Rahman M, Fukui T. Biomedical research productivity: factors across the countries. Int J Technol Assess Health Care. 2003;19:249–252. doi: 10.1017/s0266462303000229. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Amin M, Mabe MA. Impact factors: use and abuse. Medicina (B Aires) 2003;63:347–354. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]',4,'2025-10-14 06:22:17','2025-10-14 06:22:17');
